.TH ZERODDS-ROS2-SHIM 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-ros2-shim \- ROS-2 RMW shim and diagnostics
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-ros2-shim
.I SUBCOMMAND
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-set\fR \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR]...
[\fB\-\-check\-config\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-ros2-shim
is the diagnostics tool of
.BR rmw_zerodds_cpp ,
the RMW implementation that lets ROS-2 nodes use ZeroDDS as their
middleware. It is not a daemon: rcl loads the RMW library into each node.
The tool reads what the RMW reads \(em the runtime configuration
.RI ( zerodds.yaml ,
its drop-ins,
.IR include: ,
the environment) with its
.B ros2
section, see
.BR zerodds-ros2.yaml (5)
\(em and shows the mangling, the QoS profiles and overrides, discovery and
security as a node would get them. Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-ros2-bridge-1.0.md .
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B info
Show the RMW-Compat-Level and the active mangling.
.TP
.B topics
List the configured topic overrides.
.TP
.BI topic " ROS_TOPIC"
Show the DDS topic for the given ROS topic under the configured mangling,
and its override, if any.
.TP
.BI qos " PROFILE"
Show a profile of
.BR ros2.qos_profiles :
.IR default ", " sensor_data ", " services ", " parameters ", " parameter_events ,
or one the configuration adds. A field the profile leaves out keeps what the
application requests.
.TP
.B enclaves
Show the SROS2 enclave the RMW uses
.RB ( security.enclave_dir ,
env
.BR ZERODDS_SECURITY_DIR ).
.TP
.BI validate " FILE"
Validate FILE as a runtime base with its sibling FILE.d directory, as the RMW
would read it from the system directory.
.TP
.B selftest
Round-trip test (mangle + qos lookup).
.TP
.B catalog
Print the JSON catalog (Spec \(sc5.2).
.TP
.B metrics
Print the Prometheus metric-name catalog (\(sc8.2).
.TP
.B doctor
Diagnose the RMW, environment, discovery and security setup.
.TP
.B graph
Show the local participant and topic graph.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
The runtime base, with drop-ins in its sibling FILE.d directory. Without it,
zerodds.yaml and zerodds.d in the system configuration directory
(/etc/zerodds on Linux) are read, as the RMW reads them; a missing file there
means the built-in defaults. The RMW itself takes no flag; this option checks
a file before it is installed.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable: a runtime setting or a
.B ros2
key.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate the runtime configuration and its
.B ros2
section, print every value with its origin, then exit (0 valid, 1 invalid).
.PP
.BR \-\-runtime\-config ,
.B \-\-log\-level
and
.B \-\-enclave
are refused with where the value belongs:
.BR \-\-config ,
.IR "\-\-ros\-args \-\-log\-level" ,
.BR security.enclave_dir .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
Override
.BR ROS_DOMAIN_ID .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RMW_IMPLEMENTATION
Set to
.I rmw_zerodds_cpp
to route the rcl-stack through ZeroDDS.
.TP
.B ROS_DOMAIN_ID
Standard ROS-2 domain id; mapped 1:1 onto DDS-Domain-ID.
.SH FILES
.IR /etc/zerodds/zerodds.yaml ", " /etc/zerodds/zerodds.d/ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-ros2.yaml (5),
.BR ros2cli (1).
.SH AUTHORS
ZeroDDS Contributors.
